The '''1998 UEFA Cup final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match played at [[Parc des Princes]] in [[Paris]], France on 6 May 1998 as the conclusion to the [[1997–98 UEFA Cup]]. It was the first time that the UEFA Cup final was played as a single leg at a neutral venue.

The match was played between two Italian teams – [[SS Lazio|Lazio]] and [[Inter Milan|Internazionale]], commonly known as Inter. Inter won the match 3–0 to win the UEFA Cup for the third time – a joint record with [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] at the time.

==Background==
[[Inter Milan|Internazionale]] were one of the most successful Italian football teams. They had won the [[UEFA Champions League|European Cup]] twice in [[1963–64 European Cup|1964]] and [[1964–65 European Cup|1965]] and the [[UEFA Europa League|UEFA Cup]] twice in [[1990–91 UEFA Cup|1991]] and [[1993–94 UEFA Cup|1994]].<ref name="UEFACup">{{cite web |last=Stokkermans |first=Karel |title=UEFA Cup/Europa League |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablese/ec3b.html |publisher=RSSSF |access-date=20 April 2025 |date=14 June 2024}}</ref><ref name="EuropeanCup">{{cite web |last=Stokkermans |first=Karel |title=European Champions' Cup/Champions League |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablese/ec1.html |publisher=RSSSF |access-date=20 April 2025 |date=14 June 2024}}</ref>

[[SS Lazio|Lazio]] had never played in a European final before. Their previous best run was to the quarter-finals of the [[1994–95 UEFA Cup]].<ref name="UEFACup"/><ref name="EuropeanCup"/><ref>{{cite web |last=Ross |first=James M. |title=European Competitions 1994-95 |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablese/ec3b.html |publisher=RSSSF |access-date=20 April 2025 |date=5 June 2015}}</ref>

Since the inaugural edition in [[1971–72 UEFA Cup|1971–72]], the UEFA Cup final had been played over two legs on a home and away basis. From the 1997–98 season, the final would be played as a single leg at a neutral venue.<ref name="UEFACup"/>

